// Lint waiver for the vendored third-party Berkeley HardFloat IP.
//
// HardFloat intentionally uses width-narrowing assignments (e.g. dropping known
// MSBs of an exponent) and other constructs that trip the default, fatal lint.
// This is the verified upstream release (John Hauser, BSD); we do not modify it
// for style. Waive lint ONLY for those files so that our own continuant-
// coprocessor RTL stays under strict checking -- a real width/latch/unopt issue
// in *our* code will still be reported as fatal.
//
// (Comments here deliberately avoid starting a line with the tool's name, which
// the .vlt parser would otherwise treat as an inline pragma.)
`verilator_config
lint_off -file "*/third_party/HardFloat/*"
